mm/vma: avoid spurious write locks when read-locking a VMA

Extracted from the mm-new queue (wholesale) which cannot be carried as a
snapshot on the 7.4 merge-window base.  The base still uses the old
vm_lock_seq == mm_lock_seq equality test, which can falsely report a write
lock (notably when both sequence numbers are zero) and fall back to
mmap_lock.  Restore the seqcount-aware check so read locks no longer take
the slow path spuriously.

Applies to d135ab4; verified with patch --dry-run (offsets only).
